<http://data.silknow.org/object/e9b79fe7-74a6-393a-99b9-10eda52f89f5>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of woven silk and linen. The design is picked out in gold coloured silk on a lime-yellow linen background. With a floral and leaf design of stylised roses, tulips and bluebells within meandering branches and leaves in ogee formation. The sample is a lengthwise stripe that does not show a full repeat of the design."@en , "Furnishing fabric 'Golden Bough' of woven silk and linen, possibly designed by William Morris or John Henry Dearle, woven at Merton Abbey, England, 1888"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e8310622-6c05-3aff-8e8b-d0f4b672d793> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric 'Golden Bough' of woven silk and linen, possibly designed by William Morris or John Henry Dearle, woven at Merton Abbey, England, 1888"@en , "Furnishing fabric of woven silk and linen. The design is picked out in gold coloured silk on a lime-yellow linen background. With a floral and leaf design of stylised roses, tulips and bluebells within meandering branches and leaves in ogee formation. The sample is a lengthwise stripe that does not show a full repeat of the design."@en ;
